{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Physical bus",
  "exampleId": "block-physical-bus",
  "description": "The Physical bus on the left bundles three connections: the + and − terminals of a 12 V supply as pos and neg, and the 20 W heater’s heat port as heat. One bus line carries them across the sheet to a second Physical bus, flipped so its bus terminal faces left, which gives them back by name: pos and neg feed a 6 Ω load and a voltage sensor, and heat warms a 10 J/K heat capacity. Elements with the same name on the two blocks are one node, whatever order they are listed in. The same works through a subsystem: give it a physical bus port and the bus carries the elements its inside uses. Set the elements, their names and types, in each block’s properties.",
  "duration": 1,
  "revision": 0,
